# BuildKit reads this file because it sits next to the Dockerfile it is named
# after. Keeping the context small matters here: the repository root is the
# build context, and shipping the .git directory to the daemon on every build
# is the difference between a two second and a thirty second upload.
.git
.github
.playwright-mcp
docs
*.md
**/*_test.go
**/testdata
*.png
dist
